==English==

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|en|NL.|dēcubitus||lying down}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/dɪˈkjuː.bɪt.əs/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|decubitus}}

# {{lb|en|medicine}} The [[posture]] of someone in [[bed]], [[lie down|lying down]] or [[recline|reclining]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2016| author=Mariano Scaglione, Ulrich Linsenmaier, Gerd Schueller | title=Emergency Radiology of the Chest and Cardiovascular System|page=| passage=The initial recesses of the pleural cavity filled with blood effusion are declivitous; they can vary according to the '''decubitus''', whereas, with the progressive filling of the pleural cavity, blood is invariably collected in the lateral pleural spaces over the apex of the lung (apical cap): they are very large pleural effusions, in the order of about 800-1200 cc.}}
# {{lb|en|pathology}} {{ellipsis of|en|decubitus ulcer}}.

